WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Belarus has supported Russia since the start&nbsp;
of the war in Ukraine. It s provided weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.040
military bases and logistical support. 
&nbsp;

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.600
But is that support set to escalate&nbsp;
into something more active?
&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.300
In Belarus society there is a consensus that&nbsp;
we don't support this war, that Belarus army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.720
should not participate. Lukashenko also&nbsp;
feels it, also understands that if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.540
sends out Belarus troops to Ukraine, they can&nbsp;
defect, they can turn arms against him. 
&nbsp;

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:36.480
That's from my guest today. Franak Viacorka&nbsp;
is chief political advisor to Belarusian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.020
opposition leader Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya. She&nbsp;
claims to be the national leader of Belarus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:48.600
but how legitimate is her claim? And&nbsp;
how successful has her opposition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.749
been to Alexander Lukashenko's regime?
Franak Viacorka, welcome to Conflict Zone. 
&nbsp;

00:00:53.749 --> 00:01:00.240
Hello.
Mr. Viacorka, over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.040
weekend you had Russian Defense Minister Sergei&nbsp;
Shoigu in Belarus meeting his opposite number.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.680
And just a few days before that you had unnamed&nbsp;
Russian generals arriving in Minsk as well for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:17.040
various meetings. Is Russia planning an escalation&nbsp;
of the war in Ukraine with Belarus's help?
&nbsp;

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:24.120
The visits of Russian generals and officers are&nbsp;
usual things since Lukashenko came to power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:30.960
But when war has started, all the deals that&nbsp;
were signed became secret. And we don't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.540
know how much independence, how much sovereignty&nbsp;
remained in the hands of Lukashenko in the hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:42.840
of Belarusian people. We believe that every&nbsp;
visit they decide on given Belarus unit or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:52.320
Belarus sector of military complex under control&nbsp;
of Russia. Shoigu s mission to visit is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:59.940
important because it happened just after the death&nbsp;
of Minister Makei, the Foreign Minister, which was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.560
very close to Lukashenko, and it was perceived&nbsp;
by Belarusian officials as their reminder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.560
who is in charge. So Belarusian officials,&nbsp;
Belarusian officers are afraid of Moscow.
&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.700
I do want to talk about the death of Foreign&nbsp;
Minister Makei, but first I'd like to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.680
about what these visits by Russian generals&nbsp;
mean. You have, for instance, described as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.300
very dangerous development reports of Russian&nbsp;
missiles, including hypersonic missiles and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:30.180
fighter jets such as MiG 31s being stationed&nbsp;
in Belarus. What is the information you have?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:35.940
Is Russia planning large scale air assaults&nbsp;
on Ukrainian infrastructure from Belarus?
&nbsp;

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:43.860
The last missile strike that we have witnessed&nbsp;
was on November sixth from Belarus territory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:50.100
So it means already for two months there were&nbsp;
no strikes from Belarus. But for the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.380
more than 10,000 Russian soldiers arrived&nbsp;
to Belarus and they're deployed in different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:01.440
parts of our country. They're passing&nbsp;
military training. Along with the troops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:08.820
we see vehicles. We see some tanks. We see&nbsp;
some divisions of air defense systems arriving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:15.840
to Belarus. It doesn't seem they're bringing&nbsp;
attacking group of army on Belarus territory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:23.040
It seems they are bringing their army in&nbsp;
order to control the situation in Belarus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:29.400
in order to fix the Russian occupation&nbsp;
of Belarus. We really believe that Russia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:35.280
can use Belarus as a consolation prize in&nbsp;
case if it will lose the war in Ukraine.
&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.000
Are you worried that Belarusian troops might&nbsp;
be thrown into the fight in Ukraine?
&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:49.980
It's still very likely, but not next two, three&nbsp;
months. Right now, Russia doesn't have enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.980 --> 00:04:00.720
capacity nor weapons nor vehicles on Belarus&nbsp;
territory. Belarus army itself will not be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.260
conduct such operation. It needs strong backup,&nbsp;
primarily technical backup from Russia. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.000
Belarusian soldiers, they don't have morale.&nbsp;
They don't see Ukrainians as enemies. In Belarus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.040
society there is a consensus that we don't&nbsp;
support this war, that Belarus army should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:24.780
not participate. Lukashenko also feels it, also&nbsp;
understands that if he sends out Belarus troops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:31.440
to Ukraine, they can defect, they can turn arms&nbsp;
against him. There will be split of elites. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:37.620
will be new wave of protest. And he's really&nbsp;
afraid of sending Belarusian troops to Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.660
because it will, it can cost him the power.
So you're confident that with Russia's back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:49.020
the wall in Ukraine, essentially losing the&nbsp;
fight, falling behind on the battlefield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:54.300
as Jens Stoltenberg, the NATO secretary&nbsp;
general, says that President Putin is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.000
pressuring Alexander Lukashenko to commit his&nbsp;
troops into battle. You're confident of that?
&nbsp;

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.900
I think they are playing the role. It's the&nbsp;
performance. Lukashenko is playing the independent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:13.020
leader who supports Russia, and he wants to stay&nbsp;
exclusive ally for Putin because this is the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:18.660
way to stay in power, to have guarantees that&nbsp;
Putin will not come to murder him. But also for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:26.100
Lukashenko, Putin is very, very important right&nbsp;
now in order to control the internal domestic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:34.920
situation. To say that Putin is not pressurizing&nbsp;
Lukashenko, I think, let's imagine that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:42.420
is the leash and Lukashenko is the dog on the&nbsp;
leash. And Putin is trying to shorten this leash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:50.100
so much as possible, to not allow Lukashenko to&nbsp;
not leave him a space at all. This is the goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:56.040
of Putin, to create the puppet regime, satellite&nbsp;
regime, which will be doing 100% of everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:03.420
the capital Moscow will want from him.
So you had said in November that Putin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:08.640
was not interested in sending Belarusian&nbsp;
troops to Ukraine. You stand by that?
&nbsp;

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:18.000
Yes, Yes. I think it will create more problems&nbsp;
than benefits. It's not experienced army. I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.200
in the Army. I was serving in the military on&nbsp;
the border with Ukraine. It was ten years ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:30.240
But I know what is it. Lukashenko invested&nbsp;
in KGB, in the secret services that that aim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.460
to protect himself. But he never invested&nbsp;
in Belarusian army. When Belarusians will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:41.040
receive this mobilization calls, there&nbsp;
will be huge protest, huge resistance. 
&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:48.060
Because society doesn't support this war at all.&nbsp;
And Lukashenko probably told Putin about this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:55.200
Also, Lukashenko use the legend that Putin, if I&nbsp;
will send my troops, then the Poland, Lithuania,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:07:01.740
Latvia will attack me. Because you see, they&nbsp;
are preparing, they escalate. They deploy more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:07.920
troops on the border. So he used this as the&nbsp;
reasoning in order to not send out Belarusian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:13.560
troops. So they play this performance. Everyone&nbsp;
is happy. They create the pressure. They create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:18.600
the pressure on Ukraine, constant pressure&nbsp;
that this might happen. And I think that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:25.260
the threat of sending out Belarusian troops is&nbsp;
to distract a big forces of Ukrainian army.
&nbsp;

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:32.340
Help us understand Alexander Lukashenko, the&nbsp;
current leader of Belarus. Would he rather be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:37.140
on the side of President Putin or would he&nbsp;
rather be with the West, for instance?
&nbsp;

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:44.820
He will be with Putin because Putin is&nbsp;
mentally close to him. Lukashenko is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:50.940
Soviet man. He is very anti-Western democracy,&nbsp;
something that goes against his principles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:59.700
against his nature. He chose Russia and Putin&nbsp;
instead of Belarusian people in 2020. He could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:05.640
agree on dialogue with Belarusian protesters&nbsp;
two years ago, but instead he called for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:12.900
Putin's help to suppress this protest. And&nbsp;
right now, we see the tipping point of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:17.940
pro-Russianism in the head of Lukashenko.
Now, in October, Alexander Lukashenko told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:26.280
NBC in an interview that no one was closer to&nbsp;
President Putin than him. Do you read that as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:33.300
a signal to the West that he was ready to mediate&nbsp;
with President Putin, between President Putin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:40.380
the West to curtail his dependence on Russia?
Lukashenko just want to stay relevant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:45.720
to be important. He is, you know, this&nbsp;
like alpha man. He wants to be the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:50.700
everywhere. This is why he was so happy&nbsp;
when the first Minsk negotiations took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:57.780
place in 2014 and Lukashenko hosted them.&nbsp;
Lukashenko wants to be the big player. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:05.280
wants to be in the first league and also all&nbsp;
the statements about his closeness to Putin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:13.500
about nuclear weapons in Belarus in order&nbsp;
to raise the price, to raise the worth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:22.740
himself. But usually it's just a bluffing.&nbsp;
He is very poor, old, weak, insecure man.
&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.420
You talked about the death of Vladimir&nbsp;
Makei, Belarus s foreign minister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:33.600
a close confidant of Alexander Lukashenko. Did&nbsp;
Russia have anything to do with Makei s death?
&nbsp;

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:41.460
Possible. Everything is possible right&nbsp;
now. We can't exclude any of the versions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:48.780
We still didn't see the publication of the&nbsp;
document about the death of Makei with diagnosis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:54.240
It's very strange. It's one week passed, but&nbsp;
still, there is no official information. Also the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:01.680
statement from Lukashenko about the death of&nbsp;
Makei appeared many [days] after the fact was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:07.260
revealed. It means there is something behind&nbsp;
it. We see that the Belarussian officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:13.800
are very threatened. They feel that they&nbsp;
can be the next and they think this death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:20.460
could be could be just death. But also&nbsp;
it can be part of the bigger events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:25.260
bigger dynamic, we still can t see.
You talked of Russian troops in Belarus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:30.960
there to, quote, control the situation.&nbsp;
Is Belarus a hostage of Russia?
&nbsp;

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:38.160
Belarus has [been] taken hostage [by] Russia&nbsp;
and [by] Putin together. These two criminals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:45.120
they just use Belarus territory in order to attack&nbsp;
Ukraine and to revive the empire. And not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.800
Belarus, but Belarusian people are taken hostage.&nbsp;
Let's not forget that there are thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:57.060
people in jail. Hundreds of thousands were forced&nbsp;
to flee the country. In 2021 when a crackdown took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:03.300
place against Belarusian democratic forces, it was&nbsp;
a preparation for Russian war against Ukraine.
&nbsp;

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.860
You talked about the pro-democracy movement.&nbsp;
Let's talk about that. Last week, opposition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:13.080
leader Maria Kolesnikova ended up in intensive&nbsp;
care after she was transferred to hospital from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:18.180
her prison cell. She was perhaps one of the&nbsp;
last major opposition figures left inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:24.660
Belarus. Would you say her fate is a big blow&nbsp;
to the opposition movement inside Belarus?
&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.760
Maria is a big inspiration for many Belarusians,&nbsp;
especially Belarusian women. She became a symbol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:43.200
of resistance. She was leading these massive, huge&nbsp;
rallies in August and September of 2020. And right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.120
now, when we found out she is in the intensive&nbsp;
care unit, it was the big shock to all of us.
&nbsp;

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:53.220
Was it a big blow? Of course it was a big shock.&nbsp;
Was it a big blow to the opposition movement?
&nbsp;

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:05.040
Yes, it was. It was. It was a blow. It was a&nbsp;
blow. But also, we have to investigate what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:12.120
happened to her because just before ended&nbsp;
up, ended up in the hospital she was put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:17.640
in the punishment cell. This is the KGB style&nbsp;
torture cells. People are without fresh air.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:23.040
People are without communication. They could&nbsp;
be beaten there. And something something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:29.160
happened wrong to her. Perhaps there was an order&nbsp;
from Lukashenko personally to punish her.
&nbsp;

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:34.200
Doesn't all this show that the opposition&nbsp;
movement inside Belarus has been silenced?
&nbsp;

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:43.260
No, it's not silence. It changed the form of&nbsp;
resistance. There are many partisan groups. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:49.020
work in every region of the country. Most of them&nbsp;
participated in stopping the Russian trains. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:56.040
conducted sabotage on the railways in March and&nbsp;
April this year. There are thousands of people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:01.200
members of the cyber partisan groups, they are&nbsp;
paralyzing state infrastructure. And a few weeks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:08.160
ago, they hacked the Russian Oversight Committee.&nbsp;
Roskomnadzor leaked the data to journalists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:14.100
and there are many activists who put Belarusian&nbsp;
or Ukrainian flags all over the country. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:18.360
see also mass disobedience campaign, not&nbsp;
all over the country, but in big cities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:23.280
primarily when the workers of the big factories&nbsp;
refuse to do their job, for example. 
&nbsp;

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:29.460
Let's take that at face value. But hasn't&nbsp;
that invited a greater crackdown against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:35.580
them from Alexander Lukashenko?
It is indeed. Indeed. And we see right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:42.720
now the repressions bigger than in 2020. Every&nbsp;
day from 10 to 20 people are being detained and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:48.000
people not just detained, they are tortured,&nbsp;
they are harshly beaten. More activists die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:53.340
in prison. And this shock a lot. And we call&nbsp;
on the international community to react. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:59.100
call on the UN to take urgent measures.
Let's talk about numbers. The Belarusian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:06.660
human rights group Viasna claims as many as 5000&nbsp;
people are in prison due to political reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:11.040
They are not classified officially as political&nbsp;
prisoners, but they are in prison because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:15.720
their political activism. The United Nations&nbsp;
says hundreds of thousands of Belarusians are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:19.500
leaving the country and going to neighboring&nbsp;
countries. My question to you therefore is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:24.840
who is left in the country to carry out an&nbsp;
opposition against Alexander Lukashenko?
&nbsp;

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:34.740
Belarus is 9 million people country. So&nbsp;
the protest took more than 1.5 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:43.080
participants. So even if, let's say, a few&nbsp;
hundred thousand Belarusians left the country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:49.140
still we have a million to resist.&nbsp;
Also, there is a big disappointment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:57.960
big willingness to change the situation and&nbsp;
to prevent Belarus from participating in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:03.240
war. So I think people who participate in the&nbsp;
resistance right now, they did not participate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:09.480
in 2020. There are new people who reacted on&nbsp;
the fact of the war, and they resist right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:14.280
they're on the front lines and they go out&nbsp;
and they protest despite all the terror.
&nbsp;

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:19.560
You are based outside of Belarus&nbsp;
as an opposition. How effective are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:25.020
you? How many people, for instance, has your&nbsp;
movement been able to release from prison?
&nbsp;

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:34.560
We are in daily touch with Belarusian groups on&nbsp;
the ground, with local communities, with media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:42.180
with bloggers, civil journalists who spread&nbsp;
this printed samizdat leaflets, putting them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:49.860
in mailboxes. Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, leader&nbsp;
of Belarus, who won elections - She created the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:54.491
united transitional cabinet, which is like a&nbsp;
government in exile, and which gives a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.491 --> 00:15:57.660
hope and inspiration to people in the country.
We know all that. We know all that Mr. Viacorka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:02.100
but then how is that helping activists inside&nbsp;
Belarus? You admitted earlier that they keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:07.380
getting thrown into prison and that crackdown&nbsp;
has only increased since 2020. So how is your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:16.260
work outside helping them inside in Belarus?
So we pass assistance, we try to pass equipment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:21.960
where possible, we conduct information campaigns&nbsp;
to counter Russian and Lukashenko's propaganda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:27.960
primarily, but also to inspire Belarusians&nbsp;
to fight. We try to keep the morale high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:32.820
to build connection between different&nbsp;
groups, different partisan groups within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:39.120
the country. And we can lobby for more&nbsp;
international support for Belarusians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:43.440
who are still fighting in the country.
Is it not a failure of your opposition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:49.440
movement that after 2020, at that time when&nbsp;
there were massive street protests and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:55.140
seemed that the game was up for Alexander&nbsp;
Lukashenko, he has been able to hold on and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:59.940
continues to govern Belarus. Is that not&nbsp;
a failure of your opposition movement?
&nbsp;

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:08.640
Not yet. As we see, the crackdown in 2020&nbsp;
was preparation for the war. Lukashenko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:14.520
wouldn't survive without Putin. It's Putin&nbsp;
who provided him with money, with soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:22.020
with the resources back in 2020. And right now,&nbsp;
Lukashenko is paying his debt back to Putin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:27.660
It's not a failure yet, but the situation&nbsp;
became much more complex. Now we are part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:33.000
of the bigger regional geopolitical crisis.&nbsp;
Now we are fighting not just for democracy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:39.120
for democratic elections, but we are fighting for&nbsp;
very existence of Belarus statehood. And in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:43.020
to get Belarus free and independent,&nbsp;
we need the victory of Ukraine. 	
&nbsp;

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:49.260
Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, your boss, to whom&nbsp;
you provide political advice, emerged from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:53.880
2020 elections and particularly the protests,&nbsp;
the mass street protests that happened after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.880 --> 00:18:00.540
that. Now she presents herself as the leader&nbsp;
of the Belarusian opposition. Is she?
&nbsp;

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:09.300
I think she is a national leader of Belarus and&nbsp;
president elect, who won elections but didn't take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:13.920
her office because of Lukashenko and Putin.
Is she the leader of the Belarusian opposition?
&nbsp;

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:20.460
I think she is the leader of Belarus nation&nbsp;
because Lukashenko is in opposition. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.940
got more than 70% of votes, we&nbsp;
should call her the president.
&nbsp;

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.700
So she does not lead a united&nbsp;
Belarusian opposition?
&nbsp;

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:34.680
She's leading the United Democratic Forces.&nbsp;
Exactly. She united all the major groups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:40.800
traditional political parties and the new&nbsp;
groups that appeared in 2020. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:46.200
there are different ideologies, different&nbsp;
views among different politicians. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:53.580
she's absolutely the unifying figure to all of&nbsp;
those who see Belarus free and democratic.
&nbsp;

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:59.700
Let's see how unifying that is, because an opinion&nbsp;
poll by Telegram based pollster Narodny Opros&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:06.300
among opposition minded Belarusians, found&nbsp;
that the Kalinouski Regiment of Belarusian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:13.080
volunteers fighting in Ukraine was five times&nbsp;
more popular among Belarusians than Mrs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:21.900
Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya. Clearly, she's not&nbsp;
a leader of a united opposition, is she?
&nbsp;

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:28.200
This is the pollster just among activists of this&nbsp;
specific group. And Kalinouski Regiment is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:33.360
the group of military volunteers fighting&nbsp;
in Ukraine. So let's not compare, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:39.720
political leadership and fighters. And let's not&nbsp;
forget that Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya participated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:46.440
in elections she won elections -&nbsp;
multiple observers, surveys, polls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:52.380
internet voting proved that she won elections.&nbsp;
She received [inaudible] 3 million votes.
&nbsp;

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:55.800
So the Kalinouski Regiment is&nbsp;
irrelevant as an opposition group?
&nbsp;

00:19:55.800 --> 00:20:02.400
Kalinouski Regiment is the part of the democratic&nbsp;
and independence movement. They are fighters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:09.420
in Ukraine. They are fighting for liberation of&nbsp;
Ukraine, and they are they deserve a huge respect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:12.540
and we fully support everything they do.
Would you say they are popular?
&nbsp;

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:19.920
They're not popular as politicians. They are&nbsp;
popular as soldiers because they sacrifice their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:27.240
life in order to save Ukraine. They understand&nbsp;
that when Ukraine wins, Belarus wins as well.
&nbsp;

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.460
So they are not seen as a part&nbsp;
of the opposition then.
&nbsp;

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:38.280
Now they're fighters. Let's let's divide the&nbsp;
politicians and the fighters and military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:43.260
volunteers who serve in Ukrainian army. Of&nbsp;
course they are, they are playing a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:48.240
important role. And first of all, they save,&nbsp;
they preserve the good name of Belarusians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:54.660
who were seen by many Ukrainians as aggressors.&nbsp;
And Kalinouski Regiment, they prove that not all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:59.040
Belarusians are like Lukashenko, that Belarus&nbsp;
regime and people are two different things.
&nbsp;

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:03.540
Right. Let's talk about Mrs. Tsikhanouskaya.&nbsp;
You keep saying in this interview that she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:06.900
the national leader of Belarus and&nbsp;
she herself keeps calling herself the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:12.420
national leader of Belarus. But who, except&nbsp;
for Lithuania, agrees to call her that?
&nbsp;

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:20.460
Almost in every country she comes she's met&nbsp;
on the presidential level. In the parliament,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:25.260
she's always addressed as Madam President -&nbsp;
today, just in one hour, she meets Prime...
&nbsp;

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:30.840
There is no, there is no, but there is no official&nbsp;
recognition of her as the leader of Belarus.
&nbsp;

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:38.940
There is de facto recognition. There is the&nbsp;
level of protocol which defines her as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:44.580
head of state. There is no legal recognition&nbsp;
because it will take years. And we don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:49.680
these years. We don't we didn't go into this game&nbsp;
of legal recognition, we see that she is met...
&nbsp;

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:55.200
But it s more than just a game, isn't it? Because&nbsp;
Alexander Lukashenko's regime continues to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:59.640
diplomatic relations with a lot of countries,&nbsp;
particularly those in Asia and Africa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:05.880
for instance. There Alexander Lukashenko counts as&nbsp;
leader of Belarus and not Mrs. Tsikhanouskaya.
&nbsp;

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:13.380
That's true. That's true. And this is the&nbsp;
problem for us, because these nations, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:19.380
they come to the United Nations General Assembly&nbsp;
and they vote very often in support of proposals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:23.940
of Lukashenko or Russia. Yes, that s true: This&nbsp;
is why we are trying to reach out to countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:29.880
outside of the European Union. We already reached&nbsp;
out Latin American. We have some some relations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:37.560
there. We reached out to Africa, Southeast Asia as&nbsp;
well. But a lot of work to be done. But the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:42.660
important in terms of economy, in terms of trade&nbsp;
and political relationship, of course, is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:48.780
European Union, where Lukashenko is not recognized&nbsp;
as the leader. And now we are asking we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:54.360
calling and recognizing him as a war criminal.
Now, Mrs. Tsikhanouskaya has also sought to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:58.260
common cause with Ukrainians. We began&nbsp;
this interview talking about the Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:02.280
war. Let's talk about the Ukraine war. She&nbsp;
has said, and I quote, There cannot be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.520
free Belarus without a free Ukraine . Does&nbsp;
Ukraine see it in the same way as well?
&nbsp;

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:17.160
Yes, I think Ukraine sees it a little bit&nbsp;
different. They see Belarus as the guarantee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:22.320
of security, of safety, because when Lukashenko&nbsp;
stays in power, there will be constant threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.320 --> 00:23:27.660
to Ukraine like it happened in February, February&nbsp;
this year, Lukashenko promised that there will not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:34.320
be attack from Belarus territory and suddenly&nbsp;
this attack happened and Russian tanks almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:41.280
reached Kyiv from Belarus. Ukraine understands&nbsp;
the importance of having a good relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:48.120
with Belarusian people. We have 1000 kilometers&nbsp;
common border. And right now we are trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:56.640
build this relationship again. We are trying&nbsp;
to coordinate our activities and to work to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:02.580
coordinate our activities on resisting Russian&nbsp;
occupying forces. Situation in Belarus and Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:08.040
are different, but we fight the same enemy.
One final question. Mrs. Tsikhanouskaya hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.740
yet been able to meet President Zelenskyy.&nbsp;
When is that going to happen?
&nbsp;

00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:20.820
Yes. She didn't met officially, only informally&nbsp;
at one of the public events. It will happen when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:25.680
there will be willingness of Ukrainian&nbsp;
side. But she has very good relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:29.760
with the Verkhovna Rada, the Ukrainian&nbsp;
parliament. We have good relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:34.200
with Ministry of Foreign Affairs. But we&nbsp;
understand why Ukrainians don't meet her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.980
They don't want to provoke Lukashenko.
Is it also because they do not trust her?
&nbsp;

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:44.100
No, I think because there was&nbsp;
a clear sign of Lukashenko:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:44.100 --> 00:24:50.880
if Kyiv will meet Tsikhanouskaya, Lukashenko&nbsp;
can escalate the conflict against Ukraine or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:55.800
even introduce troops. So for Ukrainians right&nbsp;
now, the most important to minimize the risks.
&nbsp;

00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:59.520
When will Ukraine recognize her as&nbsp;
national leader of Belarus? Officially.
&nbsp;

00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:08.520
I think it, if Lukashenko introduces&nbsp;
troops, Belarus troops to Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:14.220
these processes will be speeded up and then&nbsp;
Ukraine can recognize Tsikhanouskaya and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:17.220
meet her. But right now, they're&nbsp;
very cautious. They don't want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:21.180
to play with fire.
It's been a pleasure talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:21.180 --> 00:25:23.880
to you. We'll have to leave it there.&nbsp;
Thank you so much for joining us today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:58.800
Franak Viacorka.

